niverse/nuclear-interactions/skein-binding-lagrangian.lean#L36-L36","doc":"Number of protons. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.SkeinBindingLagrangian.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.SkeinBindingLagrangian.mk","kind":"ctor","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/skein-binding-lagrangian.lean#L34-L34","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.SkeinBindingLagrangian","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.SkeinBindingLagrangian","kind":"structure","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/skein-binding-lagrangian.lean#L28-L52","doc":"The five-term Skein binding Lagrangian for a nucleus (p, n).\n\nThe substrate parameter is carried as its archimedean evaluation\n`q : ℝ` with `q₀ > 1` (the `1 < q` hypothesis is recorded on the\nstructure for the order-dependent terms). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:skein-binding-lagrangian","label":"def:skein-binding-lagrangian","md":"quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/skein-binding-lagrangian.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}